toolCalls.argumentsJson:
{
  "query" : "funds sent to many different recipients in a short period by wire",
  "max_results" : 5
}

{
  "description" : "one account sends multiple outgoing wires to many different domestic recipients within a few days, with no prior activity and no incoming funds"
}

{
  "alert_id" : "ALR-00004",
  "priority" : 1,
  "justification" : "C1066 had no transactions from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-21, then sent 7 CAD wires to 7 different external accounts (TX-00599, TX-00600, TX-00603, TX-00616, TX-00620, TX-00667, TX-00668) over 2026-09-22 to 2026-09-24, totalling 14637.28 CAD. It received nothing in the period. This is a sudden change in pace and recipient count from the account's own history."
}

{
  "query" : "client sending wire transfers to multiple unrelated recipients shortly after receiving funds, with no other business activity",
  "max_results" : 5
}

{
  "case_id" : "CAS-00004",
  "justification" : "C1066 had no transactions from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-21. It then sent 7 CAD wires in three days, 2026-09-22 to 2026-09-24, to 7 different external accounts (EXT-2073, EXT-2248, EXT-2104, EXT-2012, EXT-2110, EXT-2214, EXT-2023). The flagged transactions are TX-00599, TX-00600, TX-00603, TX-00616, TX-00620, TX-00667 and TX-00668, totalling 14637.28 CAD. The account received nothing in the data, so the source of the funds is unknown. Each wire is between 1217.71 and 2758.46 CAD and all are domestic (CA). This is a sudden change in pace and recipient count from the account's own history, and it matches FINTRAC indicators on wires sent to multiple unrelated beneficiaries. No similar closed cases were found to compare against. Recommend review of the source of the funds and of the seven recipients."
}
